FUN_1000_5051 (TASK 2): thread the driver-object allocator method call (DGROUP:0xd0 -> 184b) that
populates the driver-struct load-seg field -- the leg-(b) gate to both .DVRs loading.

asm 0x15071..0x15094: after FUN_1000_50c8 returns DX:AX = the .DVR file size (patch 032),
  add ax,0xf ; adc dx,0 ; rcr dx;rcr ax x4   -> AX = (size + 15) >> 4 = paragraphs
  mov bx,cs:0x5957 (driver-struct near ptr, 0x3e4 video / 0x4fa sound) ; mov cx,cs:0x595b (= DGROUP
  0x1c00) ; lcall [DGROUP:0xd0]
DGROUP:0xd0 = 0xf69:0x21bb = linear 0x1184b = FUN_1000_184b, the MEMMGR driver-object allocator (patch
023): it allocates `paras` paragraphs via the now-faithful 0a31 free-list allocator (patch 025) and writes
the allocated segment into the driver struct's load-seg field struct[0] (DGROUP:param_3[0]). The __allregs
indirect service call dropped AX/BX/CX (and Ghidra had already dropped the paragraph computation entirely,
calling the vector with a bare 0x1000), so struct[0] stayed 0 and FUN_1000_5014's AH=4B load got load_seg=0
-> both .DVRs REJECTed. Thread it faithfully: DAT_1000_5955 = the real file size (patch 032); compute the
paragraphs; call FUN_1000_184b DIRECTLY with (paras, DGROUP=0x1c00, struct near ptr) -- a direct call
threads the register args in the callee's committed order (indirect method-vector arg-threading is done
per-patch, per docs/stage1.md; DGROUP:0xd0 now also resolves to 184b via patch 031's si=0xec install,
validating the vector mechanism). Verified live: SOUNDDVR.DVR load_seg=0x3a06 (fmap wired 44 fns),
MGAVIDEO.DVR load_seg=0x3e3a (fmap wired 233 fns) -- both LOAD on the real boot path (no more REJECT).
